// Expected verdict from J. Ševčík, "Program Transformations in Weak Memory Models", PhD thesis, University of Edinburgh, 2008; checked here under sMRD.
// Load buffering with data dependencies on both sides: out of thin air.
//
// Source: Ševčík, "Program Transformations in Weak Memory Models" (PhD thesis,
//         Edinburgh 2008), §1.2 and Figure 5.1C, "prohibited".
//
// No value other than 0 appears in the program, so r1 = r2 = 1 would be created
// out of thin air; the JMM's out-of-thin-air guarantee FORBIDS it, as does sMRD.
// LB.lit is Figure 5.1A, with x := 1 in place of x := r2, which is allowed.
//
x := 0; y := 0;
{
  r1 := x;
  y := r1
} ||| {
  r2 := y;
  x := r2
}
%%
forbid (r1 = 1 && r2 = 1) [sMRD]
